[1;34mINFO  [0;39m[Claude Code] 
[1;34mINFO  [0;39m[Claude Code] ### Issues 1 & 2: LinkedTreeMap.EntrySet and LinkedTreeMap.KeySet
[1;34mINFO  [0;39m[Claude Code] 
[1;34mINFO  [0;39m[Claude Code] **Problem**: These are non-static inner classes that require an instance of the outer `LinkedTreeMap` class to be constructed. Diffblue Cover couldn't instantiate them directly.
[1;34mINFO  [0;39m[Claude Code] 
[1;34mINFO  [0;39m[Claude Code] **Solution**: Added two package-visible factory methods in `LinkedTreeMap.java`:
[1;34mINFO  [0;39m[Claude Code] - `createEntrySetForTesting()` at line 601
[1;34mINFO  [0;39m[Claude Code] - `createKeySetForTesting()` at line 647
[1;34mINFO  [0;39m[Claude Code] 
[1;34mINFO  [0;39m[Claude Code] These methods allow test frameworks to create instances of these inner classes for testing purposes.
[1;34mINFO  [0;39m[Claude Code] 
[1;34mINFO  [0;39m[Claude Code] ### Issues 3 & 4: NonNullElementWrapperList
[1;34mINFO  [0;39m[Claude Code] 
[1;34mINFO  [0;39m[Claude Code] **Problem**: The class only has a public constructor that requires an `ArrayList<E>` parameter. Diffblue Cover needs a way to construct instances without requiring arguments.
[1;34mINFO  [0;39m[Claude Code] 
[1;34mINFO  [0;39m[Claude Code] **Solution**: Added a static package-visible factory method `createForTesting()` at line 44 in `NonNullElementWrapperList.java` that creates a new instance with an empty ArrayList.
